# This CITATION.cff makes GitHub show a "Cite this repository" widget and lets
# citation managers read the software metadata. Zenodo reads .zenodo.json (not
# this file) when it mints the release DOI, so keep the two in sync.
# TODO before the release: set `version` + `date-released` to the tagged release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "el1xr_opt: an open-source optimization model for the design and operation of hybrid renewable energy systems"
abstract: >-
  el1xr_opt is an open-source mixed-integer linear optimization model, built in
  Pyomo, that co-optimizes the sizing (investment) and the operation of hybrid
  renewable energy systems coupling electricity and hydrogen, with unit
  commitment, storage, a pressure-resolved hydrogen network, and frequency
  containment reserve (FCR) provision. It extends the openTEPES modelling
  framework and ships automatic solver setup.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Erik F."
    family-names: Alvarez
    email: erik.alvarez@ri.se
    affiliation: "RISE Research Institutes of Sweden, Gothenburg, Sweden"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3862-9747"
  - given-names: "Juan F."
    family-names: Gutierrez-Guerra
    affiliation: "Institute for Research in Technology (IIT), Comillas Pontifical University, Madrid, Spain"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9441-3073"
  - given-names: Andres
    family-names: Ramos
    affiliation: "Institute for Research in Technology (IIT), Comillas Pontifical University, Madrid, Spain"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8871-1872"
version: "1.0.16"          # TODO: set to the tagged release used in the paper
date-released: "2026-07-22" # TODO: set to the actual release date (YYYY-MM-DD)
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/EL1XR-dev/el1xr_opt"
url: "https://el1xr-opt.readthedocs.io/en/latest/"
keywords:
  - optimization
  - mixed-integer linear programming
  - capacity expansion
  - unit commitment
  - hydrogen
  - electrolyser
  - battery energy storage
  - frequency containment reserve
  - sector coupling
  - Pyomo
